-60245e01b429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381438} {:answer/id #uuid "91fcd594-eba8-5b18-bdc6-28a934242f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381439} {:answer/id #uuid "a49ef088-a085-5293-b5fb-39cb0d00209e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381440} {:answer/id #uuid "204190a1-0fa4-502e-96f4-01976fa4c58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99b8d198-8410-5487-b244-b514b2208142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381437} :answer-field/id #uuid "42d2b8cc-658c-5124-be3f-b5ee81a807a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04aa90b0-83c7-56f5-b7d0-c861a0b74dfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-171841" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x-1<x.$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$\n- $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The *universal quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∀x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true on the entire universal set $U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate coincides with the universal set $U:$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=U\n$$\n\nFirst, we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1 & <x \\\\ -1 & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the final condition is true for all $x\\in Z,$ we have that the truth set of our predicate is ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, ${T}_{P}=Z.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ coincides with the universal set, the statement $∀x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152081 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "114dedd9-ed3d-5d25-8616-030ea4bd84c9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Involving Universal Quantifiers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050878 :topic/math-academy-id 2787 :topic/title "Universal and Existential Quantifiers"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4140e82-a151-54f4-a7f8-8785fc606b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149148} {:answer/id #uuid "1785aa9c-0691-5aa6-b8e7-adbb4f75858d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149149} {:answer/id #uuid "3667c61e-8f0f-5f43-a14b-7b352c7820fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149150} {:answer/id #uuid "36d4a2ca-9caa-5237-927b-d7d60bcc8a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149151} {:answer/id #uuid "634b1933-89aa-57a0-bf10-552f5845bd42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149152}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b551a35c-6f