/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3e2a498-b435-555d-acbe-67f3af373b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36477" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $6?$\n\n- ${R}_{5}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $5$\n- ${R}^{5}$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{6}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 6$ matrices over $R$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{5}[t])=5+1=6.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{5})=5\\ne 6.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6}(R))={6}^{2}=36\\ne 6.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Dimensions of Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049808 :topic/math-academy-id 2759 :topic/title "Dimension in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6425217-1196-5708-930a-3c67072d890b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150030} {:answer/id #uuid "0f145ab7-3731-53b3-b942-0890f4113dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150031} {:answer/id #uuid "3037ef58-339d-5873-b470-0ba7137c1c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident